Cancel an execution running inside a `nexora observe` server.

  Steps that have not started are never started, running steps are
  interrupted, and the execution finishes as CANCELLED. If saga is
  enabled, completed steps are compensated.

  This command talks to the observe server over HTTP
  (DELETE /api/executions/{id}) because executions live in the memory
  of the process that started them.

  Exit codes
  ──────────
  0  Cancellation requested (also when the execution was already being cancelled)
  1  Not found, already finished, or the server could not be reached
  2  Invalid arguments

  Examples
  ────────
  Cancel an execution on the local observe server:
    nexora cancel 4f3a1c2d-...

  Cancel on a remote observe server:
    nexora cancel 4f3a1c2d-... --server http://nexora.internal:9464
